data.content:
Here are the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — the markup with `@typeparam TItem`, a `@key`'d loop rendering each item's template plus Move Up/Down buttons (disabled at boundaries).

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — the `partial class` code-behind:

- Copies `Items` into a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutates the passed-in collection).
- Swap logic in `MoveUp`/`MoveDown` invokes `OnOrderChanged` with a read-only copy of the reordered list.

Usage matches your example — just use `OnOrderChanged` to receive the updated list:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> newOrder)
    {
        tasks = newOrder.ToList();
    }
}
```
